# Emergency Patient Flow

Emergency owns rapid intake, triage, stabilization, ambulance dispatch, and downstream handoff; preserve the emergency case as the source record until the patient moves to OPD, IPD, ICU, theater, referral, or discharge.

## Stage Sequence

- Arrival and quick registration.
- Case opened with chief complaint and priority.
- Triage records acuity, vitals, and routing.
- Stabilization and emergency treatment.
- Diagnostics and emergency orders as needed.
- Handoff selected, downstream flow started, and the case closed when appropriate.

## Handoffs

- Triage nurse owns intake and acuity capture.
- Emergency clinician owns stabilization and destination choice.
- System owns orchestration of OPD, IPD, ICU, or theater handoff.
- Emergency must pass source context and must not create duplicate downstream records.

## Hard Invariants

- Must not own ward beds, OPD queues, or cashier workflows after handoff.
- Must not recreate IPD when OPD already admitted the patient.
- Must preserve emergency context on the receiving module.
- May allow billing deferral when policy permits urgent care first.

## Allowed Critical Actions

- Show `Open in OPD`, `Open in IPD`, `Open in ICU`, or `Open in Theater` when links exist.
- Keep quick-registration patients visible until registration completes.
- Surface deferred billing only when the backend supports it.

